# Lightly Row (repertoire plan: lightly-row). The German folk tune "Hänschen klein", played
# without words. Only strings 3 and 2 in first position: the open string 3 (G), string 3 fret 2 (A)
# with finger 2, the open string 2 (B), string 2 fret 1 (C) with finger 1 and string 2 fret 3 (D)
# with finger 3. Form A A B A, four bars each. The teacher strums G, with D7 under bars 2, 6, 9, 10
# and 14 (the bars that sit on A and C).
title: Lightly Row
id: lightly-row
composer: Traditional German
source: German folk melody of the 19th century (Hänschen klein), instrumental; arranged for Sixstring Academy
arranger: Sixstring Academy
licence: Public domain (traditional); this arrangement is original to Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 1
tags: melody, two strings, first position, beginner
tempo: 88
time: 4/4
key: G

